WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.864
Oxford Bookworms Library. Starter.
 
00:00:04.924 --> 00:00:06.944
Police TV.

00:00:07.004 --> 00:00:11.648
By Tim Vicary. Read by Vincenzo Niccoli.
  
00:00:11.708 --> 00:00:27.200
Published and copyright Oxford University Press 2000.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:32.732
Chapter One. The Jogger.
 
00:00:32.792 --> 00:00:38.294
Dan and Sue are police officers in London.

00:00:38.354 --> 00:00:43.888
It is a Tuesday morning, and Dan is angry.

00:00:43.948 --> 00:00:46.699
What’s the matter, Dan?

00:00:46.759 --> 00:00:48.780
Sue asks.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:52.392
Look at this, Dan says.

00:00:52.451 --> 00:00:57.364
Every day someone steals money from people near the shops.

00:00:57.424 --> 00:01:00.112
We must stop this.

00:01:00.172 --> 00:01:03.281
Yes, of course, Sue says.

00:01:03.341 --> 00:01:05.752
But who is it?

00:01:05.812 --> 00:01:09.712
There is a jogger, Dan says.

00:01:09.772 --> 00:01:13.534
Every day he runs near the shops.

00:01:13.594 --> 00:01:17.415
Sometimes he runs into people.

00:01:17.475 --> 00:01:20.286
Perhaps he steals the money.

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:23.316
OK, Sue says.

00:01:23.376 --> 00:01:25.608
Let’s go to the shops.

00:01:25.667 --> 00:01:29.410
Perhaps we can see this jogger.

00:01:29.470 --> 00:01:34.622
They sit upstairs in a window over the shops.

00:01:34.682 --> 00:01:37.763
Dan has a radio.

00:01:37.823 --> 00:01:41.304
They watch the people in the street.

00:01:41.364 --> 00:01:44.684
Look! Sue says.

00:01:44.744 --> 00:01:47.115
There’s the jogger!

00:01:47.175 --> 00:01:53.086
The young man runs into an old woman, and she falls down.

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:57.226
The jogger puts his hand on the old woman's arm.

00:01:57.286 --> 00:02:00.308
I’m sorry, he says.

00:02:00.367 --> 00:02:02.500
Can I help you?

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:04.930
Here’s your bag.

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:08.142
Then a young woman shouts at him.

00:02:08.202 --> 00:02:11.514
Don’t run here! she says.

00:02:11.574 --> 00:02:15.100
It’s dangerous! Go away!
 
00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:18.278
The young man runs away.

00:02:18.338 --> 00:02:21.770
Dan talks in his radio.

00:02:21.830 --> 00:02:24.761
Quick! Stop him!

00:02:24.821 --> 00:02:27.579
He’s running up North Street!

00:02:27.638 --> 00:02:32.567
A police car stops the young man in North Street.

00:02:32.626 --> 00:02:35.568
Are you OK now?

00:02:35.628 --> 00:02:38.430
Sue asks the old woman.

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:41.281
Yes, thank you.

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:44.372
Where is that nice young woman?

00:02:44.432 --> 00:02:47.454
I can’t see her now.

00:02:47.514 --> 00:02:52.276
Have you got all your money? Sue asks.
 
00:02:52.336 --> 00:02:56.411
The old woman looks in her bag.

00:02:56.471 --> 00:02:59.706
No, I haven’t!

00:02:59.766 --> 00:03:02.356
My money’s in my purse.

00:03:02.416 --> 00:03:05.798
But my purse isn’t here!

00:03:05.858 --> 00:03:09.639
OK, Sue, Dan says.

00:03:09.698 --> 00:03:13.390
Let’s talk to the jogger!

00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:16.161
Who are you?

00:03:16.221 --> 00:03:18.842
Sue asks the young man.

00:03:18.902 --> 00:03:21.822
My name’s Peter Jones.

00:03:21.882 --> 00:03:25.252
Why? Who are you?
 
00:03:25.312 --> 00:03:28.702
We’re police officers.

00:03:28.762 --> 00:03:32.715
Why do you go running past the shops every day?

00:03:32.774 --> 00:03:34.266
Why not?

00:03:34.325 --> 00:03:35.996
I like running.

00:03:36.056 --> 00:03:38.778
OK, Dan says.

00:03:38.837 --> 00:03:41.230
Let’s look for the money.

00:03:41.290 --> 00:03:44.752
What money? Peter Jones asks.
 
00:03:44.812 --> 00:03:47.062
What are you talking about?

00:03:47.122 --> 00:03:50.964
I never take money with me when I run.

00:03:51.024 --> 00:03:56.508
Dan looks for the money but he cannot find any.

00:03:56.568 --> 00:04:01.310
Can I go now? Peter Jones asks.
 
00:04:01.370 --> 00:04:04.932
OK, Dan says angrily.
 
00:04:04.992 --> 00:04:07.424
But don’t come back!

00:04:07.484 --> 00:04:11.216
Why not? Peter asks angrily.
 
00:04:11.276 --> 00:04:12.926
I live here!

00:04:12.986 --> 00:04:15.738
And I’m not doing anything wrong!

00:04:15.797 --> 00:04:18.619
He runs away.

00:04:18.679 --> 00:04:22.942
What do we do now? Sue asks.
 
00:04:23.001 --> 00:04:27.186
Where is the old woman’s money, and her purse?

00:04:27.246 --> 00:04:30.050
I don’t know, says Dan.

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:45.700
Somebody has it. But who?

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:50.000
Chapter Two. TV.

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:55.657
Dan and Sue go back to the shops.

00:04:55.717 --> 00:05:00.614
I don’t understand, Dan says.

00:05:00.674 --> 00:05:06.988
The jogger hasn’t got the money so we must look for someone different.

00:05:07.048 --> 00:05:10.350
Look, Sue says.

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:13.661
There’s a TV camera over that shop door.

00:05:13.721 --> 00:05:16.983
Perhaps that can help us.

00:05:17.043 --> 00:05:21.986
They go into the shop and watch the video.

00:05:22.046 --> 00:05:25.090
Look, Sue says.

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:27.050
There’s the old woman.

00:05:27.110 --> 00:05:32.117
She’s getting money from the bank and putting it into her purse.

00:05:32.177 --> 00:05:36.348
Now she’s putting the purse into the bag.

00:05:36.408 --> 00:05:40.590
Stop the video there, says Dan.

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:44.252
Now, look carefully.

00:05:44.312 --> 00:05:47.654
Is anybody watching her?

00:05:47.714 --> 00:05:52.536
There are a lot of people in the street, Sue says.

00:05:52.596 --> 00:05:54.771
I’m not sure.

00:05:54.831 --> 00:05:58.216
Is it that man with the long hair?

00:05:58.276 --> 00:06:01.528
Perhaps, says Dan.

00:06:01.588 --> 00:06:03.689
Let’s go on.

00:06:03.748 --> 00:06:06.650
What happens next?

00:06:06.710 --> 00:06:09.662
They watch the video.

00:06:09.722 --> 00:06:13.463
The jogger runs into the old lady.

00:06:13.523 --> 00:06:16.804
He stops and helps her.

00:06:16.864 --> 00:06:20.867
She shouts at him and he runs away.

00:06:20.926 --> 00:06:25.152
Then a lot of people come and help the old lady.

00:06:25.212 --> 00:06:28.416
Look! Sue says.

00:06:28.476 --> 00:06:32.018
The long-haired man has her arm.

00:06:32.078 --> 00:06:37.332
Yes, but that woman has her bag, Dan says.

00:06:37.391 --> 00:06:39.702
What’s she doing with it?

00:06:39.762 --> 00:06:43.204
Oh! I can’t see!

00:06:43.264 --> 00:06:46.716
There’s a man in front of her!

00:06:46.776 --> 00:06:52.390
Listen, I have an idea, Dan says.

00:06:52.450 --> 00:06:55.018
You go to the bank tomorrow,

00:06:55.078 --> 00:06:57.200
and take some money out.

00:06:57.300 --> 00:07:01.100
Why’s that a good idea? Sue asks.
 
00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:05.300
Because we can watch you, Dan answers.
 
00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:11.000
Get a lot of money from the bank, and let everybody in the street see it.

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:13.149
Take a radio too,

00:07:13.169 --> 00:07:15.610
so you can talk to me.

00:07:15.630 --> 00:07:19.000
OK, Sue says.

00:07:19.150 --> 00:07:32.800
We can do that tomorrow morning, then.

00:07:32.900 --> 00:07:38.540
Chapter Three. Help Me! Quick!
 
00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:43.032
Next day, Sue goes to the bank.

00:07:43.092 --> 00:07:47.454
Dan is watching with another policeman, Jim.

00:07:47.514 --> 00:07:50.376
They have radios.

00:07:50.436 --> 00:07:54.888
I’m getting the money now, Sue says.

00:07:54.948 --> 00:07:57.230
That’s good, Sue,

00:07:57.290 --> 00:07:59.690
Dan says on his radio.

00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:03.106
Now let everybody see it.

00:08:03.166 --> 00:08:06.922
Sue drops some money near her feet.

00:08:06.982 --> 00:08:10.723
People in the street look at her.

00:08:10.783 --> 00:08:17.276
Look – there’s the man with the long hair! Jim says.
 
00:08:17.336 --> 00:08:19.648
He’s picking up the money.

00:08:19.708 --> 00:08:21.698
Shall I arrest him?

00:08:21.758 --> 00:08:25.821
No, wait, Dan says.
 
00:08:25.880 --> 00:08:28.062
Watch.

00:08:28.121 --> 00:08:32.954
The man picks up the money and gives it to Sue.

00:08:33.014 --> 00:08:36.046
Here you are, he says.

00:08:36.106 --> 00:08:40.080
That’s a lot of money – be careful!
 
00:08:40.140 --> 00:08:43.294
Thanks, Sue says.

00:08:43.354 --> 00:08:45.315
That’s OK.

00:08:45.376 --> 00:08:48.848
The man smiles and walks away.

00:08:48.908 --> 00:08:51.611
Have you got all the money, Sue?

00:08:51.671 --> 00:08:54.133
Dan asks by radio.

00:08:54.193 --> 00:08:58.578
Yes, it’s all here, Sue says.

00:08:58.638 --> 00:09:01.606
What can I do now?

00:09:01.666 --> 00:09:07.456
Buy some things in the shops, and then walk slowly down the street,

00:09:07.516 --> 00:09:08.988
Dan says.

00:09:09.048 --> 00:09:11.879
We’re watching you.

00:09:11.939 --> 00:09:17.724
Sue buys some apples, milk and bread.

00:09:17.784 --> 00:09:21.386
Then she walks slowly down the street.

00:09:21.446 --> 00:09:25.719
Dan and Jim watch her go.

00:09:25.779 --> 00:09:30.678
Is anybody following me? Sue asks.
 
00:09:30.738 --> 00:09:34.098
No, Dan says.

00:09:34.158 --> 00:09:38.731
There’s a woman with a baby. That’s all.

00:09:38.791 --> 00:09:43.614
Don’t follow me, Sue says into the radio.

00:09:43.674 --> 00:09:46.317
Nobody must see you.

00:09:46.377 --> 00:09:50.380
I’m turning right, into Smith Street ...

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:55.124
now I’m turning left into Peg Lane.

00:09:55.184 --> 00:09:59.396
The woman with the baby is following me ...

00:09:59.456 --> 00:10:04.168
I’m turning right, into Dale Avenue.

00:10:04.228 --> 00:10:07.150
Are there lots of people about?

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:09.030
Dan asks.

00:10:09.090 --> 00:10:12.322
No, it’s very quiet.
 
00:10:12.382 --> 00:10:14.913
Nothing is happening.

00:10:14.973 --> 00:10:18.614
Dan and Jim wait.

00:10:18.674 --> 00:10:22.196
Then Sue shouts: Be careful!

00:10:22.256 --> 00:10:26.498
Oh, help me, quick! Help!
  
00:10:26.558 --> 00:10:29.774
The jogger, Peter Jones,

00:10:29.834 --> 00:10:33.510
runs into Sue and she falls over.

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:38.782
There are apples, milk and bread everywhere.

00:10:38.842 --> 00:10:41.794
I’m sorry, says the man.

00:10:41.854 --> 00:10:43.774
Let me help you.

00:10:43.834 --> 00:10:46.966
The woman takes Sue's arm.

00:10:47.026 --> 00:10:50.818
Are you OK? she asks.
  
00:10:50.878 --> 00:10:55.230
Go away! she shouts at the man.

00:10:55.291 --> 00:10:59.519
But he sees the radio in Sue's pocket.

00:10:59.579 --> 00:11:02.408
What’s this? he asks.
 
00:11:02.468 --> 00:11:04.678
A police radio?

00:11:04.738 --> 00:11:07.460
Give me the money, quick!
 
00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:11.723
He takes the money and runs.

00:11:11.783 --> 00:11:17.626
The woman wants to run after him, but Sue holds her.

00:11:17.686 --> 00:11:20.338
Stop! she says.

00:11:20.398 --> 00:11:22.690
I’m a police officer.

00:11:22.750 --> 00:11:25.190
You must stay here!

00:11:25.250 --> 00:11:29.188
But why? the woman asks.
 
00:11:29.248 --> 00:11:31.125
I want to help you.

00:11:31.185 --> 00:11:33.166
That man has your money –

00:11:33.226 --> 00:11:35.088
I haven’t got it!

00:11:35.148 --> 00:11:39.240
Is he your friend? Sue asks.
 
00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:41.772
Where does he live?

00:11:41.832 --> 00:11:45.495
I don’t know, the woman says.

00:11:45.555 --> 00:11:48.026
I don’t know him.

00:11:48.086 --> 00:11:52.079
Who are you? Sue asks.
 
00:11:52.140 --> 00:11:54.472
Where do you live?

00:11:54.531 --> 00:12:13.000
Linda ... Linda Wilks. I live at 14, Old Street.
  
00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:18.700
Chapter Four. Man with a Knife.

00:12:20.100 --> 00:12:22.786
Dan runs up to Sue.

00:12:22.846 --> 00:12:26.497
Are you OK? he asks.
 
00:12:26.557 --> 00:12:30.106
Yes, I’m OK, she says.

00:12:30.166 --> 00:12:33.428
Go on, Dan – run!
 
00:12:33.488 --> 00:12:37.518
Sue calls a police car on her radio.

00:12:37.578 --> 00:12:41.270
Dan runs after Peter Jones.

00:12:41.330 --> 00:12:47.312
Jim, he’s turning left into Dock Lane! he shouts.

00:12:47.372 --> 00:12:49.884
Can you see him?

00:12:49.944 --> 00:12:55.685
I can see him, but he’s running very fast, Jim says.

00:12:55.745 --> 00:12:59.476
The jogger sees Jim and gets into a boat.

00:12:59.536 --> 00:13:04.368
Jim runs to the river and gets into the boat, too.

00:13:04.428 --> 00:13:07.510
Stop! Jim says.

00:13:07.570 --> 00:13:11.522
I’m a police officer – oh no!
 
00:13:11.582 --> 00:13:17.834
The jogger, Peter Jones, hits Jim and he falls into the water.

00:13:17.894 --> 00:13:21.336
The boat goes across the river.

00:13:21.396 --> 00:13:25.607
Dan helps Jim out of the water.

00:13:25.667 --> 00:13:29.569
He’s going into a cafe, Dan says.

00:13:29.629 --> 00:13:33.402
Come on – let’s run to that bridge!

00:13:33.462 --> 00:13:38.274
They go across the bridge and run to the cafe.

00:13:38.334 --> 00:13:43.588
Jim goes behind the cafe and Dan goes in.

00:13:43.648 --> 00:13:47.730
Is he in there? Jim asks on his radio.
 
00:13:47.790 --> 00:13:50.632
Yes, Dan answers.

00:13:50.692 --> 00:13:53.904
Jim – he’s coming out!

00:13:53.964 --> 00:13:56.694
Stop, says Jim.

00:13:56.754 --> 00:13:59.214
I’m a police officer.

00:13:59.274 --> 00:14:03.356
But Peter has a knife in his hand.

00:14:03.416 --> 00:14:06.618
Jim holds out his hand.

00:14:06.678 --> 00:14:10.261
Give me the knife, Peter.

00:14:10.321 --> 00:14:14.184
Stay back! Peter says.

00:14:14.244 --> 00:14:16.915
I can kill you with this.

00:14:16.975 --> 00:14:20.968
Jim can see Dan in the door behind Peter.

00:14:21.028 --> 00:14:26.107
Dan walks out of the door very slowly and quietly.

00:14:26.167 --> 00:14:29.416
Come on, Peter, says Jim.

00:14:29.476 --> 00:14:31.928
Give me the knife.

00:14:31.988 --> 00:14:35.450
Dan takes Peter's arms from behind, 

00:14:35.510 --> 00:14:38.882
and Jim takes the knife from his hand.

00:14:38.942 --> 00:14:53.500
Dan finds the money in Peter's trousers.

00:14:53.600 --> 00:14:59.025
Chapter Five. At the Police Station.

00:14:59.085 --> 00:15:03.748
I want to go home now, says Linda.

00:15:03.808 --> 00:15:07.352
My baby is hungry and tired.

00:15:07.412 --> 00:15:11.194
Do you know Peter Jones? Sue asks.

00:15:11.254 --> 00:15:15.068
Do you and Peter steal money from people?

00:15:15.128 --> 00:15:21.012
No, I don’t know him. And I never steal money.
 
00:15:21.072 --> 00:15:25.432
Do you know this woman, Peter? Dan asks.
 
00:15:25.492 --> 00:15:28.712
No, says Peter.

00:15:28.772 --> 00:15:30.674
I don’t know her.

00:15:30.734 --> 00:15:33.146
Who is she?

00:15:33.206 --> 00:15:38.541
Dan and Sue go back to their office.

00:15:38.600 --> 00:15:42.154
Does Linda work with Peter?

00:15:42.214 --> 00:15:44.366
Dan asks Sue.

00:15:44.426 --> 00:15:48.419
Yes, she does, says Sue.

00:15:48.479 --> 00:15:50.671
Watch this video.

00:15:50.730 --> 00:15:53.775
Look – there she is!

00:15:53.835 --> 00:15:56.300
She’s watching me get the money, 

00:15:56.400 --> 00:15:59.909
and now she’s talking to someone on her phone.

00:15:59.969 --> 00:16:02.920
But who is she talking to?

00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:06.101
She’s talking to Peter, of course.

00:16:06.161 --> 00:16:10.432
Now she’s following me and talking to him again.

00:16:10.493 --> 00:16:13.294
She’s talking about me.

00:16:13.354 --> 00:16:17.935
Dan and Sue speak to Linda again.

00:16:17.996 --> 00:16:21.946
Can I see your phone, please, Ms Wilks?

00:16:22.007 --> 00:16:23.903
Sue asks.

00:16:23.963 --> 00:16:25.740
My phone?

00:16:25.800 --> 00:16:28.192
Why do you want to see that?

00:16:28.252 --> 00:16:32.334
Well, it remembers a lot of numbers.

00:16:32.394 --> 00:16:36.056
Sue presses 1 on Linda’s phone.

00:16:36.116 --> 00:16:38.908
Peter’s phone begins to ring.

00:16:38.968 --> 00:16:41.310
Sue laughs.

00:16:41.370 --> 00:16:44.602
Let me ask you again, Ms Wilks.

00:16:44.661 --> 00:16:47.544
Do you know Peter Jones?

00:16:47.603 --> 00:16:54.902
Well, yes, OK. I know him. But I don’t steal money.
 
00:16:54.962 --> 00:16:58.781
Sue and Dan take Linda home.

00:16:58.840 --> 00:17:02.204
They go into her house.

00:17:02.264 --> 00:17:07.829
There’s two hundred pounds under your bed, Linda, Dan says.

00:17:07.889 --> 00:17:12.393
And look – this is the old lady’s purse.

00:17:12.453 --> 00:17:17.578
This is a nice photo of you and the baby, Sue says.

00:17:17.638 --> 00:17:19.830
But who is the man?

00:17:19.890 --> 00:17:22.514
Is he the baby’s father?

00:17:22.574 --> 00:17:27.078
OK, it’s Peter, says Linda.

00:17:27.138 --> 00:17:30.962
And yes, I do steal the money.

00:17:31.022 --> 00:17:33.374
I’m sorry, OK?

00:17:33.434 --> 00:17:35.115
No, Linda,

00:17:35.175 --> 00:17:37.878
it’s not OK, Sue says.

00:17:37.938 --> 00:17:54.000
It’s not OK at all.